[
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Dark Divinity ",
    "displayName": "Dark Divinity ",
    "notes": "*Asura have smooth, attractive forms that are impervious to mortal weapons.*\n\n- Asura can only be harmed by weapons made of Magical Materials or by Magical Abilities.\n- Attacks doing Dark Damage are reduced by 1 Heart.\n- Attacks doing Bright Damage are boosted by 1 Heart.\n- +8 Defense Rating.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "dark-divinity"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "notes": "*Lajja is surrounded by a corrupting atmosphere that crackles with malevolent mana. Those who succumb to her power are transformed into wretched slaves.*\n\nLajja benefits from an Edge on all her Aura rolls.\n- Lajja can activate her Presence at the beginning of her Turn in addition to other permitted Actions.\n- When activated, anyone in the same Battlefield Area as Lajja must attempt to resist corruption.\n- **Success:** Lajja forces your body to transform via corruptive magic:\n  - You contract an Ailment from the Corrupting Ailments Table (below).\n  - The transfiguration is painful, lose 1 Heart at the start of every Turn.\n  - If youre reduced to 0 Hearts, you become a Wretch and are now one of Lajjas Unfortunate Souls (p363).\n  - The corruption only ends if Lajja is driven off, reduced to 0 Hearts, or otherwise subdued.",
    "displayName": "Degrading Presence [L][M]",
    "shortName": "Degrading Presence ",
    "fieldName": "degrading-presence-l-m",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "displayName": "Scornful Bolt [A][M]",
    "notes": "*Lajja prefers to watch enemies buckle under her Degrading Presence. However, she'll blast stubborn or irritating foes.*\n\n- Lajja can fire her bolt at targets up to 2 Battlefield Areas away.\n- Bolts do 2 Hearts of Dark Damage.",
    "shortName": "Scornful Bolt ",
    "fieldName": "scornful-bolt-a-m",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "shameful-invigoration-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Shameful Invigoration [B]",
    "notes": "*While Lajja generally delights in the humiliation of others, she finds a strange joy in having the tables turned on her.*\n\n- If afflicted with an Ailment, Lajja will recover 1 Heart at the start of each Turn.\n- Lajja will inflict herself with a Corrupting Ailment, using her Degrading Presence, in order to regenerate lost Hearts.\n- She can end the self-inflicted Ailment at any time.",
    "shortName": "Shameful Invigoration "
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "unfortunate-souls-l",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Lajja usually travels with 4 Wretches.*\n\n- **Gear:** Wretches are unable to use equipment in any useful capacity.\n- **Abilities:** None, Wretches forget any Abilities they knew in their previous life.\n- Wretches do everything they can to remain within 1 Area of Lajja.\n- Wretches can perform an Attack Assist on someone that Lajja wishes to target with Scornful Bolt. This is the only time they will be willing to move away from Lajja.\n- Lajja can destroy and absorb a Wretch to regain 2 lost Hearts.\n- Lajja can use Wretches for Attack Assists or Recovery in addition to her other permitted Actions.",
    "displayName": "Unfortunate Souls [L]",
    "shortName": "Unfortunate Souls "
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "buzzing-mass",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*The Bizzer Swarm is not a single entity, it is made up of hundreds of tiny bugs.*\n\n- Bizzer Swarms can only be hit by Attacks made with large, broad objects or that target the entire Battlefield Area the swarm occupies. Your GM will decide which objects or strikes will make a significant impact on the swarm. Other Attacks will only kill a handful of bugs, and wont impact the effectiveness of the swarm.\n- Bizzer Swarms are immune to Ailments. A few of the bugs may be affected, but not enough to incapacitate the swarm as a whole.\n- Bizzers can fly and their Speed Rating is Fast.\n- If the Bizzer Swarm is reduced to 0 Hearts, the swarm has been killed or reduced to a harmless volume.",
    "displayName": "Buzzing Mass ",
    "shortName": "Buzzing Mass ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Engulf ",
    "notes": "*Bizzer Swarms surround a target and drain away any mana on or around them. A hungry swarm is noisy and incessant.*\n\n- Engulfing a foe requires the Bizzer Swarm to use its Action, but does not require an Attack roll.\n- Engulf can be used on a single creature or object in the same Area as the swarm. Bizzers only target creatures or items with Magical Abilities. They have no interest in non-magical entities.\n- The target is unable to use any Magical Abilities while engulfed by the Bizzer Swarm.\n- Anyone attacking the Swarm while it is using this Ability will hit the swarms target instead on an unsuccessful attempt.\n- The Swarm will do its best to follow its target, but will abandon pursuit if it becomes hazardous for the swarm, such as the target getting too close to flames or being submerged in liquid.\n- If the target somehow escapes the Swarm, they remain unable to use any magical Abilities for 1 Turn.",
    "displayName": "Engulf [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "engulf-b"
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "magic-shot",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Magic Shot ",
    "notes": "*Small, but rapid fire, magical blast.*\n\n- Once per turn the Blaster Mage can hurl small balls of mana as if a Thrown Weapon.\n- Shots do 1 Heart of Bright Damage.",
    "shortName": "Magic Shot ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Big Magic Shot ",
    "displayName": "Big Magic Shot ",
    "notes": "*An impressive blast that temporarily exhausts the Mage.*\n\nThe Blaster Mage can attempt to fire a large flaming sphere at a foe up to 2 Battlefield Areas away.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Mages Aura VS. your Deftness.\n- **Success:** The shot does 2 Hearts of Bright Damage.\n  - After firing Big Magic Shot the Mage cannot use any Magical Abilities on their next Turn.\n\nAdds 1 Bright Allegiance Point.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "big-magic-shot",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Mana Burst ",
    "notes": "*With a snap of the fingers, and some prior concentration, the ambient mana around the Blaster Mage bursts into flames.*\n\nThe Blaster Mage can attempt to blast everyone in the same Battlefield Area as them with a pyrotechnic explosion.\n- The Mage must first charge the attack by spending 1 Turn agitating the Areas ambient mana. During charging, the air around the Mage shimmers and sparkles.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Mages Aura vs. your Deftness.\n- **Success:** Everyone in the same Battlefield Area as the Mage suffers 2 Hearts of Bright Damage.\n\nThe mana in the targeted Battlefield Area is temporarily disrupted and no Magic Abilities can be used there for 1 Turn.\n\nThe Blaster Mage cannot cast Magic for 2 Turns after using Mana Burst.\n\nAdds 1 Bright Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Mana Burst [A][M]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "mana-burst-a-m"
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Mountain Of Glass ",
    "notes": "*Urarani is impossibly large and clearly unnatural, able to devastate the landscape and cover it in its odd webbing.*\n\n- Urarani is Colossal (p435).\n- **Sweep Attack:** Gooey gossamer can be spewed from the end of Uraranis tail, covering large areas in a thick crystalline webbing.\n- The web can spray up to 1 Battlefield Area away.\n- Everyone within a targeted Battlefield Area must make a Deftness Check or be completely Restrained (p270) by the web.\n- Breaking free requires you, or an ally, to use an Action and make a Might Check. Due to the webs strength, all Checks suffer a Snag.\n- Urarani can also target one of their own Strike Points but, due to their size, they are immune to the effects.\n- **Repulse Attack:** Urarani is able to blink between The Nihility and Outer World at will, and any pests crawling along its body will find themselves standing on thin air.\n- Anyone currently resting on one of Uraranis Strike Points must make a Grit Check or plummet to the ground and are Toppled (p271).\n- At the GMs discretion the fallen may also suffer an Impact Injury (p267).",
    "displayName": "Mountain Of Glass [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "mountain-of-glass-b",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "arachnid-armament",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "- Urarani can use one of the following Attacks on its Turn:\n  - **Smash:** On a successful Attack, a pincer does 3 Hearts of Damage, and can target you up to 1 Battlefield Area away.\n  - **Swipe:** Uraranis tail can target all foes located on one of its Strike Points. On a successful Attack, the tail does 2 Hearts of Damage. In addition, targets must make a successful Grit or Deftness Check or be knocked off Urarani.\n  - **Snatch:** On a successful Attack, a pincer grabs and fully Restrains (p270) you. You can attempt to escape at the beginning of each Turn by making a Might Check. Uranani can Restrain a maximum of two enemies at one time.\n  - **Crush:** If Urarani has you in its pincers, it can crush you and do 2 Hearts of damage without requiring an Attack roll.\n  - **Throw:** If Urarani has you in its pincers, it can throw you at a target up to 2 Battlefield Areas away. On a successful Attack, you and the target take 1 Heart of Damage and are Toppled (p271). On a miss, you land 2 Battlefield Areas away and are Toppled.\n  - Uraranis pincers are clumsy tools, and are incapable of delicate manipulation.",
    "displayName": "Arachnid Armament ",
    "shortName": "Arachnid Armament ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "living-nightmare",
    "shortName": "Living Nightmare ",
    "notes": "*Urarani's crystalline surface feeds off, and constantly vents, inky Dark Mana.*\n\n- Attacks doing Dark Damage are reduced by 1 Heart.\n- Attacks doing Bright Damage are boosted by 1 Heart.\n- +6 Defense Rating.",
    "displayName": "Living Nightmare ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "blubbery-hide",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Blubbery Hide ",
    "notes": "*A Chompa's skin is tough.*\n\n- +4 Defense Rating.\n- +1 Hearts Total.\n- Speed Rating is Slow.",
    "shortName": "Blubbery Hide ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "legendary-items",
    "shortName": "Legendary Items",
    "notes": "*Chosen Ones find themselves in possession of a handful of Imbued Items thanks to questing and older relatives with a habit of relic hoarding.*\n\n- Pick 3:\n  - **Red Edge:** This empowered sword is crafted from Flame Brass. It is a Master Weapon that does an additional Heart of Flame Damage upon a successful Attack.\n  - **Cleary Shield:** A Standard Shield made of Sun Gold. The bearer may also use the Parry granted by this item to nullify a Magical Ability targeted at them.\n  - **Spring Heel Boots:** Made of magical feathers which grants Supernatural Leaping (p107).\n  - **Mighty Mitten:** A mitt created from the paw of a powerful beast which grants Supernatural Might (p107).\n  - **Wooly Warm Tunic:** This endearing Extreme Weather Outfit (Cold) was woven from the legendary Wisdom Bumpos wool. Attacks that deal Flame or Frost Damage do one less Heart than usual.",
    "displayName": "Legendary Items"
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "courageous-determination",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Who needs training or experience when you have an indomitable spirit.*\n\nIf reduced to 0 Hearts, the Chosen One can attempt to shake off defeat.\n\n**Requires a Grit Check**\n- **Success:** The Chosen One springs back into action with 1 Heart restored.\n\nOnce a Session the GM can re-roll, or force a player to re-roll, if the result negatively impacts the Chosen One.\n\nThis even extends to rolls where the Chosen One isnt present. For example, to hinder the PCs from claiming a quest item that the Chosen One requires.",
    "displayName": "Courageous Determination ",
    "shortName": "Courageous Determination ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Consumed By Darkness ",
    "displayName": "Consumed By Darkness [B]",
    "notes": "*While it is sometimes possible to recognize who a demon once was, that person is gone, erased by the Blight.*\n\n- **Numb to Pain:** +2 Defense Rating.\n- **Natural Weapons:** Demons have sharpened teeth and nails. Their Unarmed Attacks strike as Standard Weapons.\n- **Shadow Sight:** Demons can see in total darkness without hindrance.\n- **Susceptible to Sunlight:** Sunlight will reduce a Demon to ash in moments.\n- Demons lose 1 Heart for every Turn they are exposed to sunlight, or the light of a fallen Star Shard (p305). Star Gems (p180) up to 1 Area away will also have this effect.\n- Demons can avoid damage from sunlight by covering their bodies in thick clothing and masks.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "consumed-by-darkness-b"
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "shadow-blight-host-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Shadow Blight Host [B]",
    "notes": "*The Shadow Blight is contagious, and a Demon's attacks can pass on the curse to the weary.*\n\n- If a Demons Attack reduces you to 0 Hearts you must check to see if you contract Shadow Blight (p374).\n- If you are immune to the Blight, you roll on the Injury Table as normal.\n- Once an enemy has been infected, the Demon will immediately switch its attention to the uninfected.",
    "shortName": "Shadow Blight Host ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Signs of the Beast",
    "displayName": "Signs of the Beast",
    "notes": "*The Demon has large, exaggerated natural weapons.*\n\n- Unarmed Attacks strike as a Mighty Weapon.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "signs-of-the-beast",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "mocking-beauty",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Mocking Beauty",
    "notes": "*The Demon possesses a haunting innocence.*\n\n- A Grit Check is required to harm or hinder them. Failing the Check momentarily mesmerizes their attacker, who misses their next Turn.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "shortName": "Mocking Beauty",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Winter's Shackles",
    "displayName": "Winter's Shackles",
    "notes": "*The Demon’s body is so cold that contact results in frostbite.*\n\n- Unarmed Attacks do +1 Heart of Frost Damage.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "winters-shackles",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "displayName": "Revolting Excess",
    "notes": "*The demon’s flesh has become tumorous and ponderously thick.*\n\n- +2 Defense Rating.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "shortName": "Revolting Excess",
    "fieldName": "revolting-excess",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "notes": "*The demon may spit acidic bile.*\n\n- Strikes as if a Thrown Weapon.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "displayName": "Caustic Spittle",
    "shortName": "Caustic Spittle",
    "fieldName": "caustic-spittle",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Synthetic ",
    "displayName": "Synthetic [B]",
    "notes": "*The drone is a mechanical being.*\n\n- Immune to Fatigue, Starvation, and Suffocation.\n- Immune to toxins that target living tissue which are ingested, inhaled, or injected.\n- Drones are powered by an engine that feeds on ambient mana. If the flow of mana into the engine is disrupted then they will cease to function.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "synthetic-b"
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "mad-machine-b",
    "shortName": "Mad Machine ",
    "notes": "*As a result of overexposure to mana, the Drone now has thoughts and feelings it wasn't designed to process.*\n\n- The Drone can enter at will into an erratic, rampaging state that:\n  - Grants a Minor Bonus (+2) to Might rolls.\n  - Provides +1 Heart of Damage to physical Attacks.\n  - Causes a -2 to their Defense Rating, due to reckless flailing.\n  - Attempting to exit this state requires the Drone to make a successful Insight Check.",
    "displayName": "Mad Machine [B]",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "displayName": "Labor Frame ",
    "notes": "*The Maintenance Drone's body is engineered for industrial work.*\n\n- +4 Defense Rating.\n- +1 Hearts Total.\n- Maintenance Drones are Slow.\n- Mechanical limbs strike as Standard Weapons.",
    "shortName": "Labor Frame ",
    "fieldName": "labor-frame",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Imposing Figure ",
    "notes": "*War Drones stand tall on the battlefield.*\n\nThe War Drone is a Large Species.",
    "displayName": "Imposing Figure [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "imposing-figure-b"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "displayName": "Combat Shell ",
    "notes": "*War Drones have a shell made from unyielding Gleysian Alloy.*\n\n- +6 Defense Rating\n- +1 Hearts Total",
    "shortName": "Combat Shell ",
    "fieldName": "combat-shell",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "arcane-afterburner",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*War Drones take up advantageous positions using their mana thrusters.*\n\nWar Drones have Supernatural Leaping.",
    "displayName": "Arcane Afterburner ",
    "shortName": "Arcane Afterburner "
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "advanced-sensor-suite-a",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*War Drones have an array of scanners that help them identify all possible threats.*\n\n- War Drones can sense all targets up to 100 feet away or, during a Fight, the entire Battlefield.\n- They can distinguish between organic and synthetic targets.\n- They are immune to the Obscured Battlefield Condition (p251).\n- They can see through physical barriers, such as walls or smoke.\n- Their hearing is comparable to that of an average human.",
    "displayName": "Advanced Sensor Suite [A]",
    "shortName": "Advanced Sensor Suite ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "notes": "*Concentrated mana can be expelled towards ranged targets.*\n\nMana Blast: In addition to its other permitted Actions, the War Drone can direct an Attack that does 2 Hearts of Bright Damage towards a target up to 2 Battlefield Areas away.",
    "displayName": "All Range Attack System ",
    "shortName": "All Range Attack System ",
    "fieldName": "all-range-attack-system",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "morphic-armament-a",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Morphic Armament [A]",
    "notes": "*One of the War Drone's arms has a built-in weapon with multiple configurations.*\n\n- At the start of a Turn the War Drone can configure its weapon arm into one of 3 modes:\n  - **Bulwark Mode:** Serves as a Large Shield.\n  - **Crusher Mode:** Strikes as a Master/Mighty Combo Weapon.\n  - **Wire Mode:** Strikes as a Lash/Ark Combo Weapon.\n  - The weapon is treated as Magical Material (Gleysian Alloy).",
    "shortName": "Morphic Armament ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "colloid-corpus",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Colloid Corpus ",
    "notes": "*Goops are oddly colored, semi-solid masses that are animated by mana trapped within them.*\n\n- Goops are gelatinous creatures devoid of defined shape or limbs.\n- They cannot hold or use objects.\n- They are able to squeeze under doors and into small spaces.\n- They cannot be restrained by ropes or similar bonds due to their amorphous body.\n- Goops dissipate in water and lose 1 Heart each Turn they spend at least half submerged in liquid.",
    "shortName": "Colloid Corpus ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "inexorable-sludge-b",
    "shortName": "Inexorable Sludge ",
    "displayName": "Inexorable Sludge [B]",
    "notes": "*Goops are sticky and sluggish.*\n\n- Their tacky surfaces allow them to traverse walls and ceilings.\n- Goops are Slow.",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Corrosive Contact ",
    "notes": "*Caustic bodies destroy and consume.*\n\n**Attaching to Prey:**\n- Goops can attempt to stick onto a target in the same Battlefield Area as them. You can avoid this with a successful Deftness Check.\n- If a Goop attaches successfully to you it causes a Serious Burn from the Caustic/Burning Injury Table (p267), and again on every subsequent Turn until the Goop is dislodged or destroyed.\n\n**Removing Goop:**\n- You can use your Turn to attempt to remove a Goop. This requires a successful Might Check.\n\n**Attacking an attached Goop:**\n- If striking an attached Goop, the Goop’s prey takes the damage if the Attack roll is failed.\n\n**Corroding objects:**\n- Goops can damage objects softer than Very Hard by attaching to them. They corrode at a rate of 1 Heart per Turn.\n- The one exception to this is glass, which they cannot corrode.",
    "displayName": "Corrosive Contact [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "corrosive-contact-b"
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "giga-body-b",
    "shortName": "Giga Body ",
    "notes": "*The Giga Gruun are 15 feet tall, and mostly bone and muscle.*\n\n- Giga Gruun are Massive.\n- **Sweep Attack:** Flailing arms or Tusks strike as Arc Weapons.\n- **Focus Attack:** Stomps and headbutts strike as Mighty Weapons.",
    "displayName": "Giga Body [B]",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "giga-hide-l",
    "shortName": "Giga Hide ",
    "notes": "*These biological war machines were manufactured to withstand severe punishment, both physical and magical.*\n\n- +6 Defense Rating.\n- Giga Gruun gain an Edge on Checks or Contests that involve resisting the effects of Magic Abilities.\n- Spell disrupting patterns woven into the Giga Gruuns skin reduce the Damage caused by offensive Magic Abilities by 1 Heart.",
    "displayName": "Giga Hide [L]"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Furious Rampage ",
    "displayName": "Furious Rampage ",
    "notes": "*Giga Gruun are devoid of discipline or grace, they fight with relentless brutality.*\n\nIn addition to its other permitted Actions, the Giga Gruun can make a bonus Combat Action.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "furious-rampage"
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Sun Blotter ",
    "displayName": "Sun Blotter [B]",
    "notes": "*The Grim Wing casts a massive shadow.*\n\n- Grim Wings are Massive (p434).\n- **Sweep Attack:** Tail and wings strike as Arc Weapons.\n- **Focus Attack:** Talons and fangs strike as Mighty Weapons.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "sun-blotter-b",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Bio-Sorcerous Body ",
    "notes": "*Constructed to revel in ceaseless battle.*\n\n- +8 Defense Rating due to its toughened skin and feathers.\n- The Grim Wing is resilient to pain and regains 1 lost Heart every Turn.\n- The Grim Wings eyes can see in blinding light and total darkness.",
    "displayName": "Bio-Sorcerous Body [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "bio-sorcerous-body-b"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "skybound-destroyer-b",
    "shortName": "Skybound Destroyer ",
    "displayName": "Skybound Destroyer [B]",
    "notes": "*Burning eyes can fire concentrated mana.*\n\nIn addition to its other permitted Actions, a Grim Wing can use:\n\n**Beam:**\n- The Attack can target an enemy up to 2 Battlefield Areas away. A hit deals 3 Hearts of Bright Damage and forces you to make a Might Check or be Toppled.\n\n**Spray:**\n- The Grim Wing can target a Battlefield Area up to 1 Area away. A single Attack roll is made and compared to the Defense Rating of everyone in the targeted Area. Those hit suffer 1 Heart of Bright Damage."
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "immaculate-uniform",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Immaculate Uniform ",
    "notes": "*True maids take pride in their appearance, yet understand their uniform must be fit for the job at hand.*\n\n- Murder Maids wear Light Armor combined with an Appealing Outfit.\n- +2 Defense Rating.",
    "shortName": "Immaculate Uniform "
  },
  {
    "displayName": "Tidy Battle Stance [A]",
    "notes": "*Battle Butlers are elegant combatants.*\n\n- Every Battle Butler has a Weapon Type they are proficient in. Using their Chosen Weapon provides:\n  - +1 Attack Bonus.\n  - +2 Defense Rating.\n  - A Battle Butlers Chosen Weapon has a Custom Ability (p160).",
    "shortName": "Tidy Battle Stance ",
    "fieldName": "tidy-battle-stance-a",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "notes": "*Surviving enemies, like dirt and grime, are considered intolerable filth.*\n\n- Once per Turn the Murder Maid can expend 1 Heart to re-roll a failed Attack.\n- Murder Maids have a Minor Bonus (+2) on Checks and Contests connected to keeping things tidy.",
    "displayName": "Out Damn Spot ",
    "shortName": "Out Damn Spot ",
    "fieldName": "out-damn-spot",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "notes": "*Murder Maids zip from place to place with little effort.*\n\nMurder Maids have Supernatural Leaping.",
    "displayName": "Back Forth Without Fuss ",
    "shortName": "Back Forth Without Fuss ",
    "fieldName": "back-&-forth-without-a-fuss",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Expeditious Manner ",
    "displayName": "Expeditious Manner [B]",
    "notes": "*The Battle Butlers move with alacrity.*\n\nBattle Bulters are Fast.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "expeditious-manner-b",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "unruffled-monotony-a",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Unruffled Monotony [A]",
    "notes": "*A Battle Butler prefers to prevent a disaster rather than mop up afterwards.*\n\nA Battle Butler can use their Action in an attempt to thwart any weapon Attack made in the same Battlefield Area as them.\n- This Ability must be declared before an Attack roll is made.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Butlers Grit vs. the attackers Might.\n- **Success:** The attacker falters and cannot act on their Turn.\n  - Battle Butlers have a Minor Bonus (+2) on Checks and Contests connected to keeping things on track.",
    "shortName": "Unruffled Monotony ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "mischievous-minuscule-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Lalka fit in the palm of your hand.*\n\nLalkas are Tiny.",
    "displayName": "Mischievous Minuscule [B]",
    "shortName": "Mischievous Minuscule "
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "elemental-vex",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Elemental Vex ",
    "notes": "*Lalkas have a smidgen of elemental power.*\n\n**Breeze Lalka:**\n- Can summon a powerful breeze to:\n  - Push over, or move, an object no larger than 2 Inventory Slots.\n  - Distract or annoy you, providing an Attack Assist to an ally.\n  - Attempt to blow something out of your hand or Topple you (p271).\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- Lalkas Aura VS. your Might.\n\n**Mud Lalka:**\n- Can sling grime pulled from their bodies as if a Thrown Weapon.\n- Adds 1 Bright Allegiance Point.",
    "shortName": "Elemental Vex "
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Arcane Beleaguerment ",
    "notes": "*When all else fails, Lalka will sacrifice themselves to temporarily delay their foe. They can even coordinate their efforts with their fellow Lalka.*\n\nLalka can hurl themselves at you in a self-destructive attempt to slow you down.\n- Whether the attempt is successful or not, the Lalka is destroyed.\n\n**Breeze Lalka:**\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- Lalkas Deftness vs. your Grit.\n- **Success:** The Lalka forces its way into an orifice and evaporates. You are Ballooned (p268) for 1 Turn.\n\n**Mud Lalka:**\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- Lalkas Deftness VS. your Might.\n- **Success:** The Lalka splatters itself over your leg and hardens. You are Petrified for 1 Turn.\n  - Up to 3 Lalka can attempt this Ability together, each Lalka adds +2 to their Contest roll and prolongs the effect by 1 Turn.",
    "displayName": "Arcane Beleaguerment [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "arcane-beleaguerment-b"
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "battlefield-domination-l",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Oppressors demonstrate poise and skill far beyond that of ordinary warriors.*\n\n- Oppressors get +2 Bonus to their Defense during a Fight.\n- Once per Turn, the Oppressor gets an additional Attack if they reduce a foe to 0 with their first Attack.\n- The Oppressor may attempt Attack Stunts (p255) without making a wager.\n- Oppressors are immune to the Terrified Ailment.",
    "displayName": "Battlefield Domination [L]",
    "shortName": "Battlefield Domination ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "war-gods-might-a",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "War Gods Might [A]",
    "notes": "*The Oppressor's strength is appropriately overwhelming.*\n\nOppressors have Supernatural Might.",
    "shortName": "War Gods Might "
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "impatient-destroyer-a",
    "shortName": "Impatient Destroyer ",
    "notes": "*The Oppressor can rapidly close the distance on their chosen enemy.*\n\nOppressors have Supernatural Leaping.",
    "displayName": "Impatient Destroyer [A]"
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Wall Of Blades ",
    "notes": "*Wild, uncertain, or amateurish attacks against the Oppressor invite their wrath.*\n\nThe Oppressor may immediately make an opportunistic Attack against anyone who fails a Melee Attack on them.",
    "displayName": "Wall Of Blades ",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "wall-of-blades",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "never-surrender",
    "shortName": "Never Surrender ",
    "displayName": "Never Surrender ",
    "notes": "*Pushing an Oppressor to their very limit runs the risk of invigorating them.*\n\nIf reduced to 0 Hearts, the Oppressor can attempt to reinvigorate themselves.\n\n**Requires a Grit Check**\n- **Success:** The Oppressor restores 4 Hearts, and is ready to fight.\n- **Failure:** They will die, but have enough time left to say something to the people who have managed to do the deed.\n\nThis Ability cannot save them from inescapable death, like being crushed by a stone block.",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "notes": "*The Pedagogue has compressed their magical tools into a single worn device. While it resembles an ornate bracelet or pendant, it is so much more.*\n\nThe Magician’s Apparatus has the following functions:\n**Wizard Sight:** The Apparatus sends out a subtle mana pulse that scans the environment every few seconds allowing the Pedagogue to ‘see’ even if in complete darkness or physically blinded.\n**Mage Flight:** The Apparatus creates a cushion of mana for the Pedagogue to rest upon, allowing them to fly and hover.\n**Spell Force:** With the use of an Action the Pedagogue is able to manipulate, push, or lift objects up to 15ft away.\n- The force can be as delicate or strong as an adult human hand.\n- If used in a Check or Contest, the bearer’s Insight is used, instead of Might or Deftness.\n- This Ability can be used to Attack a foe up to 2 Battlefield Areas away. This requires an Attack roll, does 2 Hearts of Damage, and leaves the target Toppled.\n**Infinite Reference:** The Apparatus is constantly scrying and absorbing knowledge for the Pedagogue to use at a later date. With the use of an Action the Pedagogue can attempt to retrieve useful information about a particular person, place, thing, or concept they may not have heard of before.\n\n**Requires an Insight Check**\n- **Success:** They have gained functional knowledge of the subject referenced: known weaknesses, probable location or intentions, etc.\n\nAdds 2 Bright Allegiance Points.",
    "displayName": "Magicians Apparatus ",
    "shortName": "Magicians Apparatus ",
    "fieldName": "magicians-apparatus",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "congruent-consciousness-m",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*The Pedagogue's mind is active, even when they sleep, their dreams replaced with rational thought. There is work to be done, after all.*\n\n- Benefits from an Edge on all Insight rolls.\n- Can perform an extra Action per Turn if used to perform one of the Pedagogues Magical Abilities, but the same Ability may not be used twice in the same Turn.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "displayName": "Congruent Consciousness [M]",
    "shortName": "Congruent Consciousness ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "barrier",
    "shortName": "Barrier ",
    "displayName": "Barrier ",
    "notes": "*Mana is constantly flowing within and around the Pedagogue. It is a simple matter for them to turn it into a flexible, flowing defensive field.*\n\n- The Barrier must be destroyed before the Pedagogue can be targeted directly.\n- The Barrier has:\n  - Defense Rating 16\n  - 3 Hearts\n- The Barrier is active at the beginning of each Fight (unless Ambushed!).\n- The Pedagogue can use an Action to restore the Barrier if destroyed.\n- Adds 1 Bright Allegiance Point."
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "bind-a-m",
    "shortName": "Bind ",
    "displayName": "Bind [A][M]",
    "notes": "*The Pedagogue is able to coerce dark mana into thick cords that can entangle.*\n\nThe Pedagogue can use an Action to attempt to Bind foes in the Battlefield Area they currently occupy, or any adjacent to it.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Pedagogues Insight VS. the Might (or Deftness if higher) of those inside the targeted Area.\n- **Success:** Cords of dark mana snare and wrap around any target that lost the Contest. All their limbs are Restrained (p270).\n\nRestrained targets, or assisting allies, may use an Action to make a Might or Deftness Check to cut the binding. To do this, a sharp implement is required.\n- The cords dissolve immediately if they are no longer binding anyone.\n\nAdds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "blast",
    "shortName": "Blast",
    "notes": "*The Pedagogue is able to agitate large clusters of mana to create a powerful explosion. This spell is a favorite way to clear away rabble.*\n\nThe Pedagogue may use Blast to target a Battlefield Area adjacent to the one they currently occupy.\n- The Pedagogues Insight vs. the Deftness of those inside the targeted Area.\n- Anyone in the targeted Area that loses the Contest takes 2 Hearts worth of Bright Damage.\n- The GM may decide that easily destructible objects, such as glass bottles, are destroyed if caught in the area of the Blast.\n- Adds 1 Bright Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Blast"
  },
  {
    "notes": "*The Pedagogue is able to weigh down a target by smothering them in dense mana.*\n\nThe Pedagogue can use an Action in an attempt to Burden a target up to 2 Battlefield Areas away.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Pedagogues Insight vs. the targets Might.\n- **Success:** Heavy globs of dark mana cling to the target, making them Overburdened (p270).\n\nBurdened targets, or assisting allies, may use an Action to make a Might Check to tear away the accumulated mana.\n\nAdds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Burden [A][M]",
    "shortName": "Burden ",
    "fieldName": "burden-a-m",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Doggone Good Sense ",
    "displayName": "Doggone Good Sense ",
    "notes": "*Mundymutts hear and smell better than any other species in the Outer World.*\n\n- Mange have an Edge on all Insight Checks and Contests involving hearing or sense of smell. For example, tracking or sniffing out a hidden or disguised individual.\n- Mange can smell mana and can tell when magic of any kind is being used, or was recently used, nearby. They can even discern between Bright and Dark mana.\n- Things not native to Outer World (Dimensional Strays, Asuras, Devas, etc.) smell off and make them uneasy. This could explain their infamous dislike of the Rai-Neko.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "doggone-good-sense",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "strays-step-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Strays Step [B]",
    "notes": "*Bandit pups learn fast that stragglers are left behind.*\n\nMange Bandits are Fast.",
    "shortName": "Strays Step "
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "canine-pounce-a",
    "shortName": "Canine Pounce ",
    "displayName": "Canine Pounce [A]",
    "notes": "*Proudhounds can bound into battle.*\n\n- Proudhounds have Supernatural Leaping (p107).\n- **Leap Attack:** After leaping, Proudhounds can use their Action to deliver a shuddering blow that:\n  - Gains a +2 to hit.\n  - Does +1 Heart of Damage.\n  - Drains 1 Heart from the Proudhound whether the Attack lands or not.",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "fearsome-growl-b",
    "shortName": "Fearsome Growl ",
    "notes": "*An especially intimidating bark.*\n\nOnce per Fight the Proudhound can use their Turn to snarl and bark in an attempt to scare adversaries within a range of 1 Battlefield Area.\n\n**Requires a Grit Contest**\n- **Success:** You are Terrified (p271) until the Proudhound is dealt with.",
    "displayName": "Fearsome Growl [B]",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "living-dead-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Skelefolk are not subject to the afflictions that plague the living.*\n\n- Immune to Fatigue, Starvation, Suffocation, and aging.\n- Immune to toxins that target living tissue which are ingested, inhaled, or injected, except\n- The eyes and tongue are still subject to attacks that target living tissues. Destroying them demotes them to a Skeleman.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Living Dead [B]",
    "shortName": "Living Dead ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "pull-yourself-together-skelemaster",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*You can’t keep an evil Skelemaster down.*\n\n- When reduced to 0 Hearts, or less, their bones clatter to the ground, but over the next 3 Turns they will reform, all Hearts restored.\n- The GM may decide a crushing or obliterating attack prevents Self-Assembly. Otherwise, youll need to take a Turn to shatter the skull to prevent reanimation.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Pull Yourself Together ",
    "shortName": "Pull Yourself Together "
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "hollow-eyed-servants-a-m",
    "shortName": "Hollow Eyed Servants ",
    "displayName": "Hollow Eyed Servants [A][M]",
    "notes": "*Skelemen keep a hollow-eyed vigil for their masters.*\n\n- Skelemasters are instantly aware of anything a Skeleman or Clacking Cranium within 1 mile of them sees or hears.\n- The ability is limited to a 1 mile radius from the Skelemaster.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point."
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "pull-yourself-together-monarch",
    "shortName": "Pull Yourself Together - Monarch",
    "displayName": "Pull Yourself Together - Monarch",
    "notes": "*The Skelemonarch will return.*\n\n- When reduced to 0 Hearts, or less, their bones clatter to the ground, but over their next 3 Turns they will reform, all Hearts restored.\n- The Skelemonarchs glowing Soul Stone is revealed while they are inert (20 Defense, 1 Heart).\n- It can only be sundered with an Imbued Weapon, an Artifact, or a destructive magical Ability.\n- Only if the Soul Stone is Sundered (p263) will the Skelemonarch crumble to dust.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point."
  },
  {
    "notes": "*Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.*\n\n- Skelemonarchs are instantly aware of anything a Skelemaster, Skeleman, or Clacking Cranium within 1 mile of them sees or hears.\n- Skelemonarchs are also able to telepathically communicate with any Skelemen or Skelemasters within a 1 mile range.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Hollow Eyed Servants - Monarch",
    "shortName": "Hollow Eyed Servants - Monarch",
    "fieldName": "hollow-eyed-servants-monarch",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Macabre Aura ",
    "notes": "*Mana swirls around the Skelemonarch, deflecting or absorbing inbound attacks.*\n\n- + 6 Defense Rating.\n- Can Parry once per Round as a Standard Shield (p169).\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Macabre Aura [A]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "macabre-aura-a",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "displayName": "Skelemancy",
    "notes": "*Skelemonarchs’ dark magic, characterized by grand gestures and ominous laughter.*\n\nOnce per Turn, the Skelemonarch can use one of the following:\n\n**Skull Shot:**\n- The Skelemonarch can attempt to throw a cackling mana skull at you from up to 2 Areas away.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Skelemonarch’s Aura vs. your Deftness.\n- **Success:** You take 2 Hearts of Dark Damage.\n\n**Bone Brambles:** Twisted bone spikes erupt in the Battlefield Area the Skelemonarch occupies, giving it the Isolated Condition.\n\nAdds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "shortName": "Skelemancy",
    "fieldName": "skelemancy",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "notes": "*The Skelemonarch's hatred of flesh is so strong that it lashes out at anyone nearby.*\n\nThe Skelemonarch can attempt to convert you, or any other organic creature in its Battlefield Area, into one of its lifeless subjects.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\n- The Skelemonarchs Aura VS. your Grit.\n- **Success:** Your body begins to wither and becomes Putrefied, you lose 1 Heart per Turn.\n  - The Curse wont manifest if you make a successful Grit Check when your Hearts reach 0, or the Putrefied Aliment is removed by another Ability, or the Skelemonarch is slain.\n  - If the Curse is blocked you will return to physical normalcy in a few moments, though you still suffer from any lost Hearts if the Fight is still in progress.\n  - Failing the Grit Check at 0 Hearts results in your flesh melting away. You have been transformed into a subservient Skeleman, or Skelemaster if you are Rank 5 or higher.\n- **Failure:** You resist and are immune to the Curse for 24 hours.\n  - Bio-Mechanoids, and other forms of inorganic life, are immune to the Curse.\n\nAdds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "displayName": "Curse Of The Skull [L][M]",
    "shortName": "Curse Of The Skull ",
    "fieldName": "curse-of-the-skull-l-m",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "tragic-behemoth",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Tragic Behemoth ",
    "notes": "*Even though their shape is in constant flux, a Shadow Beast is always frightfully large.*\n\n- Shadow Beasts are Massive (p434).\n- **Sweep Attack:** Long neck and limbs strike as Arc Weapons.\n- **Focus Attack:** Stomps and bites strike as Mighty Weapons.",
    "shortName": "Tragic Behemoth ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Surging Darkness ",
    "notes": "*The Shadow Beast's body moves like liquid darkness, yet remains concrete.*\n\n- The Shadow Beast is Fast.\n- +6 Defense Rating, the Shadow Beasts density repels weak Attacks.\n- The Shadow Beast is able to climb sheer surfaces with lease, and is unhindered by the Isolated Battlefield Condition.",
    "displayName": "Surging Darkness [B]",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "surging-darkness-b",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "notes": "*Faces contorted in fear and woe ebb and flow along the surface of the Shadow Beast, emitting pitiful cries as they surface and submerge. Hear them and despair.*\n\nIf you come within 1 Battlefield Area of the Shadow Beast, you must attempt to resist its horror.\n\n**You require a Grit Check**\n- **Failure:** You contract the Dispirited Ailment (p269). The Ailment lasts until the Shadow Beast has left your sight.\n- **Success:** You are immune to this Ability for 24 hours.\n\nAdds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Howls Of The Lost [B]",
    "shortName": "Howls Of The Lost ",
    "fieldName": "howls-of-the-lost-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "fieldName": "forsaken-shadow",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Shadow Beasts fear light, knowing instinctively that it is their only real weakness. Darkness, no matter how malicious, only comforts them.*\n\n- If the Shadow Beast comes within 2 Battlefield Areas of a Star Gem, or other source of sunlight, it is automatically Terrified (p271). The Beast will retreat from the source if at all possible.\n- Attacks inflicting Bright Damage receive a +1 Damage bonus against the Shadow Beast.\n- Attacks inflicting Dark Damage do not harm the Shadow Beast, and will actually restore 1 lost Heart.\n- Light from a mundane source, such as a lantern or torch, only serves to aggravate the Shadow Beast. They know it is only a pale imitation of what they truly fear.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Forsaken Shadow ",
    "shortName": "Forsaken Shadow ",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "shortName": "Caustic Miasma ",
    "displayName": "Caustic Miasma ",
    "notes": "*The Shadow Beast is followed by a fog of malignantly charged Dark Mana that eats away at flesh, steel, and bone.*\n\n- Any Area the Shadow Beast occupies gains the Harmful Battlefield Condition (p250). The Shadow Beast itself is immune to this effect.\n- Long exposure to this Ability may damage structures and unattended objects at the GMs discretion.\n- This Ability is negated by the presence of a Star Gem, or other form of sunlight, emanating from a source up to one Battlefield Area away from the Shadow Beast.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "caustic-miasma"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "your-worst-friend-b",
    "shortName": "Your Worst Friend ",
    "displayName": "Your Worst Friend [B]",
    "notes": "*The cloud cannot stray far from the creature whose negative demeanor brought it into existence.*\n\n- A Cloud can be inadvertently created by any creature capable of being miserable or unpleasant. The progenitor could be another Adversary or GMC.\n- The Cloud is able to fly and hover, but it cannot move more than 20 ft (or 2 Battlefield Areas in a Fight) away from its progenitor.\n- If the Cloud loses all its Hearts, it vanishes with an angry hmph! It will reform near its progenitor in 24 hours, assuming they are still alive.\n- It vanishes instantly if its progenitor has been slain.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point."
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "displayName": "Made Of Sterner Puff ",
    "notes": "*The cloud is more solid than you'd expect.*\n\n- Thanks to its diminutive size and Ability to solidify itself, the Tiny Unhelpful Cloud has a +2 on its Defense Rating.\n- The Tiny Unhelpful Cloud can solidify its body while floating around an object and try to grab or push over an object. Snatched items are usually dropped in very inconvenient locations.\n- If the item is being held or carried, its bearer may prevent it from being snatched by making a successful Might Check.\n- The Tiny Unhelpful Cloud is unable to carry or manipulate objects that are larger or heavier than 3 Inventory Slots.",
    "shortName": "Made Of Sterner Puff ",
    "fieldName": "made-of-sterner-puff",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "personal-rainy-day",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*A tiny storm cloud is still a storm cloud.*\n\n- The Tiny Unhelpful Cloud can hover above someone its host is openly hostile towards and pelt them with localized rainfall and tiny lightning bolts. This is supremely annoying and often a bit painful.\n- Doing so requires the Clouds Action for a Turn and causes the target to have a Snag on all Rolls until the end of their next action.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Personal Rainy Day ",
    "shortName": "Personal Rainy Day "
  },
  {
    "notes": "*Thanks to a combination of a large pack and numerous pockets and pouches, the Undead Peddler always seems to have something useful for sale.*\n\n- The Undead Peddler always has 12 Slots worth of uncannily useful items when encountered. These items vary from peddler to peddler, but they always manage to be useful for the location they are wandering in.\n- A few might stock potent imbued items or relics, though they are wary about showing these to the wrong type of customer.\n- Most Undead Peddlers are wired with explosives that they can detonate instantly when they are worried about being exploited. The explosives are powerful enough to destroy them and all their wares. Anyone within 1 Battlefield Area of the exploding Peddler feels the effect of the Bomb (p178).\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Corpse Commodities [B]",
    "shortName": "Corpse Commodities ",
    "fieldName": "corpse-commodities-b",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "displayName": "Insectoid Form - Oppressing Swarm",
    "notes": "*A cloud of flying bugs that move by the will of a single mind.*\n\n- The Swarm can only be hit by Attacks that affect entire Battlefield Areas, or weapons that are large enough to swat a significant number of bugs.\n- The Swarm is immune to Ailments. A few bugs may be afflicted, but the rest are unaffected.\n- The Swarms Speed Rating is Fast.\n- The Swarm has 2 Insectoid Aspects.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "shortName": "Insectoid Form - Oppressing Swarm ",
    "fieldName": "insectoid-form-oppressing-swarm",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "insectoid-form-unseen-crawler",
    "modType": "strength",
    "displayName": "Insectoid Form - Unseen Crawler ",
    "notes": "*A scuttling bug that silently observes, Bellzuub's favorite Form.*\n\n- The Unseen Crawler is Tiny (p434), although noticeably larger than a regular insect.\n- The Crawler receives an Edge on all rolls related to stealth or avoiding detection.\n- The Crawler can climb and cling to surfaces like a spider.\n- The Crawler has 2 Insectoid Aspects.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "shortName": "Insectoid Form - Unseen Crawler "
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "displayName": "Insectoid Form - Bladed Hunter ",
    "notes": "*A humanoid mantis creature that is deadly in battle.*\n\n- The Hunters raptorial legs strike as Dual Wielding (p254) Quick/ Master Combination Weapons..\n- Or one of the chitinous legs can also act as a Standard Shield.\n- This form can forgo the raptorial forelimbs in favor of arms that can manipulate standard Gear.\n- The Hunter has 3 Insectoid Aspects.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "shortName": "Insectoid Form - Bladed Hunter ",
    "fieldName": "insectoid-form-bladed-hunter",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "shortName": "Insectoid Form - Crushing Giant ",
    "displayName": "Insectoid Form - Crushing Giant ",
    "notes": "*A huge arachnid shape meant to overwhelm and terrify foes.*\n\n- The Crushing Giant is Massive (p434).\n- **Sweep Attack:** Legs can flail to strike as Arc Weapons.\n- **Focus Attack:** Legs can stomp to strike as Mighty Weapons.\n- The Giant has 2 Insectoid Aspects.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "insectoid-form-crushing-giant",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "displayName": "Unshaped ",
    "notes": "*The Unshaped are ideas or concepts attached to a cluster of primordial magic. When they wish to interact with reality, they must manifest into a physical form.*\n\n**Formation:**\n- Unshaped can only adopt one Form at a time. Forms can be imitations or monstrous distortions of Outer World creatures. Mimicry is never perfect, and the observant will pick up on this ‘tell’.\n- Each Form can be further modified with Aspects. Aspects grant the manifestation additional features. The number of Aspects allowed is dependant on the chosen Form.\n- Unshaped can shift between forms at will or, during a Fight, at the beginning of each Turn. They can also change their chosen Aspects in a similar fashion.\n- After manifesting into their first Form the Unshaped’s Heart Total is set. It is not altered or replenished if the Unshaped changes Forms during a Fight.\n- If reduced to 0 Hearts, the manifestation is destroyed and the Fight ends. The Unshaped is not dead, but it will take a few hours before it is able to reform.\n\n**Combat Values & Aptitudes:**\n- Scores for Combat Values and Aptitudes are provided. Alter these as required depending on the Form and Aspects that the Unshaped chooses.\n- Adds 2 Dark Allegiance Points.",
    "shortName": "Unshaped ",
    "fieldName": "unshaped",
    "modType": "strength"
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "modType": "strength",
    "fieldName": "the-verminous-incantation-b",
    "shortName": "The Verminous Incantation ",
    "notes": "*Those seeking to deal with Bellzuub with any sort of finality must perform a ritual to force him into a permanent state. The Verminous Incantation has been passed among arcane scholars for centuries. Hermit spell casters, town elders, and large libraries could provide this information to curious adventurers.*\n\n**Ritual:**\n- 1. First create and present an Enhanted Lure to summon Bellzuub, he will typically investigate within 1-3 days.\n- 2. Once Bellzuub manifests, utter the incantation to lock him into his current physical Form. The bind will last for a period of 24 hours.\n- 3. Finally, if you slay Bellzuub and burn his body whilst he is locked in physical Form, he will remain dead. Reality reacts to an Unshapeds death with a series of unusual events. In Bellzuub's case, plagues of confused insects torment nearby Settlements for several weeks.\n\n**Enchanged Lures:**\n- A Lure must be something that an insect would be naturally drawn to, but made with Magic Materials or Additives by someone with an Advanced Crafting Discipline.\n- The nature of the Lure will also dictate the Form Bellzuub chooses to manifest in. For example: a mixture of honey and Mistake Sugar might conjure a swarm of ant-like creatures, a Stargem lantern might attract a giant moth- like manifestation, and the bloom of a magical flower might summon an unusual buzzing insect.\n- Adds 1 Bright Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "The Verminous Incantation [B]"
  },
  {
    "displayName": "Chittering Puppetry ",
    "notes": "*Bellzuub can animate the recently slain by infesting them with insects, enabling him to make pawns of pauper and prince alike.*\n\n- Bellzuub can make a Puppet of anyone he has killed.\n- Bellzuub can control multiple Puppets, but the combined Ranks of the animated individuals must not exceed 9. For example, a pair of Puppets who are Rank 4 and Rank 5, nine Puppets who are all Rank 1, or a single Puppet of Rank 9. Rank 0 characters count as Rank 1 for calculation purposes.\n- Bellzuub can release an individual from his control at any time to take over a new corpse. The abandoned host collapses in a lifeless heap.\n- Individuals under Bellzuubs control retain all abilities and knowledge but have no will of their own. Puppets mimic the living effectively, although those close to a host might notice that they are out of sorts.\n- Bellzuub is aware of everything his Puppets experience.\n- Wounding a Puppet, or exposing them to fire, will reveal the bugs hiding inside their body.\n- If a Puppet is reduced to 0 Hearts, they are destroyed and the swarm will evacuate the host, only to wither and die shortly afterwards.\n- Colossal Creatures, artificial beings, and creatures that lack a solid body are immune to this Ability.\n- Adds 1 Dark Allegiance Point.",
    "shortName": "Chittering Puppetry ",
    "fieldName": "chittering-puppetry",
    "modType": "strength",
    "subtext": ""
  },
  {
    "subtext": "",
    "fieldName": "brotherhood-of-pests-a",
    "modType": "strength",
    "notes": "*Bellzuub is not the father of all vermin, he is more like a beloved uncle. All insects and scavenging mammals will answer his call; while they are not willing to follow his orders, they are happy to share gossip.*\n\n- If Bellzuub, or one of his Puppets, has been located in an area or town for at least a week he will be able to establish a loose network of vermin informers.\n- The network will keep Bellzuub informed of any local events, or important discussions, that transpire in the presence of a bug or small rodent.\n- Bellzuub will be aware of anything the PCs have done, or discuss doing, if he makes a successful Insight Check. If privy to this knowledge he will be prepared.\n- Adds 1 Bright Allegiance Point.",
    "displayName": "Brotherhood Of Pests [A]",
    "shortName": "Brotherhood Of Pests "
  },
